content.text:
The rate import is written on both sides and `bin/e2e` is now building and running in the background. I'll be notified when it finishes, then fix whatever it turns up.

- **Server:** a new endpoint, `POST /api/sheets/{sheetId}/rates/import`, in `RateController`. A new `ImportRatesService` reads each non-blank line as grade,rate,from,to, where from and to may be missing or blank. It checks every line with the rate form's rules (grade A, B or C; a rate up to 999.99 with at most two decimals; real dates; to not before from). If any line fails, it gives a 422 error saying which line. Otherwise it sets each line in order through the existing `RateService.set`. That replaces a rate for the same grade and from-date and writes `RATE_SET` and any rollups, just as the form does. All lines go through in one transaction, so a refusal writes nothing to the store or the audit file.
- **Front end:** the Rates panel now has an import box, with these test ids:
  - `import-rates`, the text box;
  - `import-rates-submit`, the button;
  - `import-rates-set`, the count of rates set, cleared while an import runs;
  - `import-rates-error`, the error, which also covers an empty paste.

  After an import succeeds, the people screen re-reads the sheet. The box clears when another sheet is loaded.

